- this directory contains the skeleton for the simple regex
  Finite-State-Machine based matcher final test.

- Files include:

labsearchstr:		pre-compiled sample solution of searchstr
summarisetests:		my C-Tools unit test summariser

Part1/README:		readme file for Part 1
Part1/checkregex.[ch]:	check regex for banned combinations - skeleton
Part1/testcheck.c:	Unit test program for checkregex module
Part1/.cbuild:		Custom CB config file

Part2/README:		readme file for Part 2
Part2/fsm.[ch]:		Finite State Machine module - skeleton
Part2/testfsm.c:	Unit test program for fsm module
Part2/.cbuild:		Custom CB config file
Part2/token.[ch]:	Token related definitions and utilities

Part3/README:		readme file for Part 3
Part3/makefsm.[ch]:	RE to FSM convertor module - skeleton
Part3/testmakefsm.c:	Unit test program for makefsm module
Part3/match.[ch]:	regex string matching and reporting code
Part3/testmatch.c:	Unit test program for match module
Part3/searchstr.c:	Match a regex to a string on the command line
Part3/.cbuild:		Custom CB config file

BONUS/copyin:		Shell script to copy *.[ch] files from PartN/
BONUS/.cbuild:		Custom CB config file.

lib/*:			many .h files and a library libsupport.a
			containing many pre-compiled modules (eg
			regex.o, checkregex.o, fsm.o, makefsm.o and
			a support module called emphasize.o).
			Note that the source code for lib is not
			available to you.


Possible invocations of labsearchstr you might like to try:

./labsearchstr 'hello' "hell helloo there"
./labsearchstr 'hello' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr '^hello' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr '^hello' "helloo there"
./labsearchstr 'he?llo?' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr 'he?llo?' "hll halloo there"
./labsearchstr '^he?llo?' "hll halloo there"
./labsearchstr 'h[eua]l+o*' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr '^h[eua]l+o*' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr 'h[eua]l+o+' "hell halloo there"
./labsearchstr '^h[eua]l+o+' "hellooooo halloo there"
